    "body": "> What do you mean with CSS size? By default canvas pixels are treated as CSS pixels so this is a bit confusing. I guess you are trying to make it match display pixels instead?\n\nYou're right it's all very confusing, I amended the OP to hopefully clarify. While canvas treats the unit `1px` as one bitmap pixel when the CTM is identity, the CSS applied on the `<canvas>` element may change how the canvas size is displayed, and then the device pixel ratio (and zoom levels) will scale it again. See [this QA](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2588181/canvas-is-stretched-when-using-css-but-normal-with-width-height-attributes) and its 112 dupe targets.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
