    "updated_at": "2026-05-06T20:49:31Z",
    "body": "> Can't the `canvas.width = w; canvas.height = h` lines be set every time during the `onpaint` event, so that you're up to date?\n\nSure, but something needs to trigger the `paint` event when the canvas size changes, that's why the size-change-detection code is in the `requestAnimationFrame` handler. You could do this:\n\n```\nfunction update_state() {\n  const [w, h] = canvas.getDevicePixelContentBoxSize();\n  if (canvas.width != w || canvas.height != h) {\n    // Trigger paint event\n    canvas.requestPaint();\n  }\n  // update application/scene state but do not draw\n  if (canvas_should_be_redrawn) {\n    canvas.requestPaint();\n  }\n  // update state in a continuous loop\n  requestAnimationFrame(update_state);\n}\nrequestAnimationFrame(update_state);\n\ncanvas.addEventListener('paint', evt => {\n  const [w, h] = canvas.getDevicePixelContentBoxSize();\n  canvas.width = w;\n  canvas.height = h;\n  // canvas draw code\n});\n```\n\n... but I'm not sure why that would be preferable.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/4392040269/reactions",
